riscos-mesa: SDL 2's own test programs
======================================

testgl2, testgles, testgles2 and loopwave from SDL 2.26.0, built from their
unchanged source against riscos-mesa's SDL2 (which has OpenGL, OpenGL ES
1.1 and 2.0 through its RISC OS video driver, and sound through its RISC OS
audio driver). The GL tests each open a 640x480 desktop window with a
spinning cube.

Needs SharedUnixLibrary and ARMEABISupport.

!TestGL2    desktop OpenGL
!TestGLES   OpenGL ES 1.1
!TestGLES2  OpenGL ES 2.0 shaders (slower: shaders run on the CPU)
!LoopWave   sound: plays a sample over and over through SharedSoundBuffer
            (it mixes with other programs' sound). It has no window, so it
            runs single-tasking; press Escape to stop it. Its Output file
            says which audio driver was used ("riscos" is the new one).

Escape or the close icon quits. SDL's test options work too if you run the
!RunImage from a command line, for example --fullscreen, --vsync or
--info all.

The programs' log (the GL version, and the frame rate when they quit) goes
to the file Output inside each application. Please report those figures.

Sources and the porting guide: docs/porting/sdl2.md in the riscos-mesa
repository. Licence: zlib (see each application's Licence file).
